<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Etiuni</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 780 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A confederation of tribes around Lake Sevan and the Ararat plain, whose conquest by Urartu opened the way for the founding of Erebuni, the forerunner of Yerevan.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known only from Urartian royal inscriptions. In the 9th century BCE the name Etiuni covered a cluster of tribal lands north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-sevan">Lake Sevan</a> and the plain beneath <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-aragats">Mount Aragats</a>, which the expanding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a> treated as one hostile country.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union was a loose alliance of local chiefdoms living from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herding, farming and bronze and iron working, with hill fortresses of the kind still visible around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-sevan">Sevan</a>. Urartian texts list captured people and livestock in the thousands, showing a populous region but saying little about its institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argishti-i">Argishti I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a> conquered much of Etiuni in a series of campaigns in the early 8th century BCE, and his successor Sarduri II campaigned there again. Captives were resettled at the new fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erebuni">Erebuni</a>, founded in 782 BCE, and the region became an Urartian province.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 900 BCE – 780 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:2.39%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 780 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Etiuni tribal union</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-840&amp;focus=etiuni" aria-label="Etiuni on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5780 732 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Etiuni lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6077 1051h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6100 988h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6100 988h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Armenia. <a href="/atlas?year=-840&amp;focus=etiuni">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

